  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and consultation to reimagine the futures of education in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO Dakar will conduct research and multi-stakeholder consultations on the futures of education in Africa as a component of the follow-up to the Transforming Education Summit (TES) and the African Union Year of Education 2024. The second Continental Report on SDG4 and CESA 16 &#x2013; 25 will be developed, launched and disseminated. A series of multi-stakeholder consultations will be organized to inspire reflections and discussions on what it means to transform education in Africa on the occasion of the AU Year of Education and the evaluation of the CESA 16 &#x2013; 25. The results of the consultations will inform the next continental strategy of education in Africa, the Summit of the Future in 2024 and World Social Summit in 2025, while generating ideas for accelerating progress towards the SDG4 targets and for the post-2030 global education agenda.</narrative>
  </description>
